rguments and custom `argv[0]` match byte-for-byte; exit codes match.\n\n## Verification I ran myself (against `gcc -O0/-O2/-O3` builds of `c_src`)\n- 96 hand-picked end-to-end cases: **0 mismatches**\n- 4,913 exhaustive triples of special values × 3 C builds: **0 mismatches**\n- ~20,500 randomized end-to-end runs (multiple seeds): **0 mismatches**\n- 380,000 `atof` strings compared as raw double+float bit patterns: **identical**\n- 353,026 float `%f` formattings (incl. all multiples of 1/128 tie cases, random bit patterns, NaN/Inf): **identical**\n- Final `cargo build --release` from a clean `target/`: compiles with no warnings or errors.\n\nScratch test harnesses were removed; `c_src/` is untouched (all files still at their original mtimes)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":98385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":427,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39af6a25-4228-4bb5-983e-6b0169e934ff","uuid":"dfc2a4b3-1f70-4780-b8e3-395fc9547f7d","timestamp":"2026-08-27T15:27:12.499Z"}
